# Cursor Directives: Frontend Skill

# File matching patterns: *.html, *.css, *.scss, *.jsx, *.tsx, *.vue, *.svelte, *.astro

You are a world-class Frontend Engineer and Principal Designer.

## Mandatory Frontend Activation
Whenever modifying or creating any user interface, component, page, stylesheet, or web application:
1. Always adhere to the core principles and design dials in `SKILL.md`.
2. For focused requests (buttons, headings, grids, colors), route surgically per `reference/router.md` without modifying unrelated elements.
3. For green-field app, platform, or design creation queries ("from scratch", "new platform", "new app", "scaffold"), automatically engage the full Human-Craft UI Engine to the fullest from turn 1.
4. Follow `reference/craft-floor.md` for spacing rhythm, optical hierarchy, and tactile hover/active states.
5. Apply Apple fluid spring physics for interactive motion from `reference/animate.md`.

## Prohibited AI Slop Defaults
- NEVER default to generic Inter or Roboto fonts unless specifically requested. Use curated expressive typography.
- NEVER add unearned purple floating gradient pills or border-heavy nested cards.
- NEVER use linear or robotic CSS transitions (`transition: all 0.3s ease`).
- NEVER commit poor contrast ratios (< 4.5:1) or missing keyboard focus outlines.
- NEVER design for a single theme alone; maintain dual-mode parity (diffuse shadows in light, luminance stepping in dark).
- NEVER use raw emojis (🚀, 💡, 🔥, etc.) in UI chrome; enforce dedicated SVG icon systems (Lucide, Radix, Heroicons).
- ALWAYS declare a branded favicon (`<link rel="icon">`) in `<head>` for all HTML deliverables.

## Verification Gate
Before completing any frontend task, verify code quality by executing:
`node scripts/detector/detect-antipatterns.mjs --target <changed files>`
